Context of the x86-shina run
The configuration under which the translator ran, and every
interpretation that a model of the run uses. The Interpretations
section of backend/README.md explains each interpretation; a comment
at the top of a model lists what is specific to it.

Configuration
  initial-enum cur_mode=LongMode
  initial-bool has_adx=true
  initial-bool has_bmi2=true

Interpretations
  Each Sail call or construct is replaced by the HOL term below it. a,
  b, ... stand for its arguments, s for the state before it, s' for the
  state after it and s0 for the state at the start of the instruction.

  AF
    ~> word (bitval (read AF s))
  AF = a
    ~> s' = write AF (bit 0 a) s
  CF
    ~> word (bitval (read CF s))
  CF = a
    ~> s' = write CF (bit 0 a) s
  GPR[a]
    ~> read (registers :> (element (iword a))) s
  GPR[a] = b
    ~> s' = write (registers :> (element (iword a))) b s
  OF
    ~> word (bitval (read OF s))
  OF = a
    ~> s' = write OF (bit 0 a) s
  PF
    ~> word (bitval (read PF s))
  PF = a
    ~> s' = write PF (bit 0 a) s
  SF
    ~> word (bitval (read SF s))
  SF = a
    ~> s' = write SF (bit 0 a) s
  ZF
    ~> word (bitval (read ZF s))
  ZF = a
    ~> s' = write ZF (bit 0 a) s
  read_simd(128, a)
    ~> read (SIMD128 (Simdreg (iword a) Lower_128)) s
  read_simd(256, a)
    ~> read (SIMD256 (Simdreg (iword a) Lower_256)) s
  undefined : 1 word
    ~> v, where the whole relation is ?v:1 word. ...
  undefined : 16 word
    ~> v, where the whole relation is ?v:16 word. ...
  undefined : 32 word
    ~> v, where the whole relation is ?v:32 word. ...
  undefined : 64 word
    ~> v, where the whole relation is ?v:64 word. ...
  write_simd(128, a, b)
    ~> s' = write (SIMD128 (Simdreg (iword a) Lower_128)) b s
  write_simd(256, a, b)
    ~> s' = write (SIMD256 (Simdreg (iword a) Lower_256)) b s
